Usage:
  gohard check [flags] [PATH...]

Parse and analyze VHDL; with --sim, run testbenches.

Flags:
      --allow-empty        exit 0 when no VHDL files are found
      --coverage           simulate and write statement, branch and PSL cover coverage to .gohard/coverage (lcov)
      --define NAME=VALUE  define a conditional-analysis identifier (overrides defines:); repeatable
      --env NAME=VALUE     set a variable GETENV sees in simulation (overrides simulation.env.vars); repeatable
      --format FORMAT      diagnostic output format: text, json, sarif or junit (default text)
      --real-env           let simulation read the real clock and environment; the run is marked non-reproducible
      --repro FILE         rerun the simulation recorded in a repro file
      --seed N|random      simulation seed; 0 keeps declaration order
      --sim                also elaborate and simulate testbenches
      --strict             exit 1 on any warning (hints never fail a run)
      --tb NAME            run only the testbench NAME

Global flags:
  -h, --help         show help
  -p, --jobs N       run at most N parallel jobs (output never depends on N)
      --output FILE  write standard output to FILE (a temp file, then rename)
